# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale fi
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as aamupaiva [10:00, 12:00)
# (CLDR morning2).
# Surface: aamupäivällä, the adessive of aamupäivä "forenoon" (the stretch
# between mid-morning and noon, which Finnish names separately from aamu --
# see the five-band note in chronologia/dayparts.py).
# Source: Wiktionary, "aamupäivällä": adessive singular of "aamupäivä".
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aamup%C3%A4iv%C3%A4ll%C3%A4
# CLDR 47 fi names this period "aamupäivällä" in the format-wide day periods.
# The same surface is the am meridiem (clock_meridiem_am.voc): the band lies
# wholly before noon, so both readings agree.
aamupäivällä
